1
00:01:10,668 --> 00:01:13,261
What do you want?
Beer.

2
00:01:13,786 --> 00:01:16,061
All I got is piss-warm Chango.

3
00:01:16,266 --> 00:01:17,619
That's my brand.

4
00:01:36,186 --> 00:01:37,460
This is damn good.

5
00:01:39,626 --> 00:01:42,379
I'd say this is the best beer
I've ever had.

6
00:01:43,946 --> 00:01:45,095
Actually....

7
00:01:45,386 --> 00:01:46,501
Need anything there?

8
00:01:46,866 --> 00:01:48,902
I'm just glad to be alive right now.

9
00:01:49,826 --> 00:01:52,545
I was up a few towns away.
You know Saragosa?

10
00:01:53,106 --> 00:01:56,337
I was at a bar there.
Not unlike this one, they serve beer.

11
00:01:56,546 --> 00:01:58,298
Not as good as this, but close.

12
00:01:59,946 --> 00:02:02,540
And I saw something
you wouldn't believe.

13
00:02:03,426 --> 00:02:05,860
I'm sitting there by myself.

14
00:02:06,066 --> 00:02:07,419
Now, this bar...

15
00:02:08,746 --> 00:02:10,145
...was full of lowlifes.

16
00:02:14,066 --> 00:02:16,136
I mean,
not like this place here.

17
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:17,785
No, I mean bad.

18
00:02:18,026 --> 00:02:19,698
Like they were up to no good.

19
00:02:21,546 --> 00:02:23,741
I'm all by myself.
I like it that way.

20
00:02:24,226 --> 00:02:26,581
Meanwhile, things are going on.

21
00:02:27,186 --> 00:02:30,781
Under-the-table kinds of things.
Not too obvious...

22
00:02:31,186 --> 00:02:32,778
...but not too secret either.

23
00:02:34,826 --> 00:02:35,895
So...

24
00:02:36,746 --> 00:02:37,656
...l'm sitting...

25
00:02:40,666 --> 00:02:42,702
...and in walks...

26
00:02:42,946 --> 00:02:46,097
... the biggest Mexican
I have ever seen...

27
00:02:46,346 --> 00:02:48,098
... Iike he owns the place.

28
00:02:48,346 --> 00:02:51,179
Nobody knew what
to make of him or think of him.

29
00:02:51,706 --> 00:02:54,061
But there he was, and in he walked.

30
00:02:54,826 --> 00:02:56,225
He was dark too.

31
00:02:57,786 --> 00:02:59,777
I don't mean dark-skinned.

32
00:03:00,386 --> 00:03:01,660
This was different.

33
00:03:01,906 --> 00:03:04,374
It was as if he was always
walking in a shadow.

34
00:03:04,866 --> 00:03:06,936
Every step he took
towards the light...

35
00:03:07,146 --> 00:03:10,661
...just when you thought his face
would be revealed, it wasn't.

36
00:03:11,106 --> 00:03:13,301
It was as if the lights dimmed...

37
00:03:13,506 --> 00:03:14,416
...just for him.

38
00:03:23,346 --> 00:03:24,938
So this guy...

39
00:03:26,546 --> 00:03:28,184
... takes a seat at the bar...

40
00:03:28,426 --> 00:03:30,656
... orders a soda, sits back,
says nothing.

41
00:03:30,906 --> 00:03:32,134
He ordered a soda pop?

42
00:03:32,706 --> 00:03:34,617
I wasn't interested in his drink.

43
00:03:35,186 --> 00:03:37,256
I was interested in what he carried.

44
00:03:38,346 --> 00:03:41,304
Some sort of a suitcase,
kind of heavy.

45
00:03:41,546 --> 00:03:44,458
And he sat that thing beside him
as if it were his girl.

46
00:03:47,186 --> 00:03:49,416
Then, all of a sudden,
the bastard spoke.

47
00:03:50,506 --> 00:03:53,782
You know he was talking business
because he upset the bartender.

48
00:03:54,026 --> 00:03:55,982
Especially when he mentioned....

49
00:03:56,746 --> 00:03:58,577
He said something like:

50
00:04:00,226 --> 00:04:02,023
" Bitch" or...

51
00:04:02,746 --> 00:04:03,701
..." Bucho."

52
00:04:09,906 --> 00:04:11,419
That's what it was.

53
00:04:11,706 --> 00:04:12,900
Bucho!

54
00:04:15,746 --> 00:04:17,896
He pissed off the bartender plenty.

55
00:04:18,146 --> 00:04:20,535
Some of those unsavory characters...

56
00:04:20,786 --> 00:04:24,461
...not like these boys, but real scum,
they got pissed too.

57
00:04:24,866 --> 00:04:28,222
Started pulling guns and knives.
Starting some shit.

58
00:04:28,746 --> 00:04:30,020
Now, the stranger...

59
00:04:30,266 --> 00:04:31,779
...he bolts off of the barstool.

60
00:04:32,026 --> 00:04:34,381
He dives into the middle of the room
with his case.

61
00:04:34,586 --> 00:04:35,382
Dives right in.

62
00:04:35,626 --> 00:04:39,062
I don't know what he does there, but in
two shakes the suitcase is open...

63
00:04:39,306 --> 00:04:43,265
...and he's pulled out the biggest hand
cannon I've ever fucking seen.

64
00:05:03,906 --> 00:05:05,419
That was just the beginning.

65
00:05:06,506 --> 00:05:10,215
You just stood there?
You didn't run for cover or join in?

66
00:05:10,706 --> 00:05:12,537
I was frozen stiff.

67
00:05:12,946 --> 00:05:14,982
All I could do was watch this...

68
00:05:18,946 --> 00:05:20,743
...thing tear the place apart.

69
00:05:20,986 --> 00:05:22,101
It was amazing.

70
00:05:25,546 --> 00:05:29,255
Cutthroat scumbags were coming forward
and dying much-deserved deaths.

71
00:05:29,786 --> 00:05:33,256
Don't get me wrong, this was no
class-act group like you got here.

72
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:34,701
Not at all.

73
00:05:34,946 --> 00:05:37,301
No, these guys were world-class turds.

74
00:05:37,546 --> 00:05:40,060
I'm sorry, but they got
what they deserved.

75
00:05:40,386 --> 00:05:42,024
It was Judgment Night in that place.

76
00:05:45,786 --> 00:05:47,538
He grabs one of these guys...

77
00:05:47,786 --> 00:05:49,424
...the only guy still breathing.

78
00:05:49,666 --> 00:05:51,816
He starts getting
information out of him.

79
00:05:52,026 --> 00:05:53,584
And I knew by the whispering...

80
00:05:53,826 --> 00:05:55,942
... this guy was giving up the goods.

81
00:05:56,186 --> 00:05:58,746
Spilling his guts.
Confessing the world.

82
00:05:58,946 --> 00:06:00,777
He told that stranger everything.

83
00:06:02,146 --> 00:06:03,420
Everything?

84
00:06:09,186 --> 00:06:12,462
Can I get a cleaner mug?
This one's dirty.

85
00:06:14,146 --> 00:06:15,340
Fuck you.

86
00:06:16,546 --> 00:06:18,377
It's the cleanest one I got.

87
00:06:26,786 --> 00:06:28,014
So anyway...

88
00:06:28,866 --> 00:06:30,015
...without warning...

89
00:06:30,226 --> 00:06:31,978
...without any hint or preview...

90
00:06:32,466 --> 00:06:34,058
...the stranger whips around...

91
00:06:34,306 --> 00:06:35,421
...and he sees...

92
00:06:36,146 --> 00:06:36,976
...me.

93
00:06:37,626 --> 00:06:38,945
You saw his face?

94
00:06:39,586 --> 00:06:40,860
His face?

95
00:06:41,186 --> 00:06:42,141
No.

96
00:06:43,626 --> 00:06:44,945
His eyes.

97
00:07:02,466 --> 00:07:04,422
And he didn't do anything to you?

98
00:07:04,626 --> 00:07:07,094
Not really. He turned
to the guy on the floor.

99
00:07:09,746 --> 00:07:11,259
Stranger shot him...

100
00:07:12,386 --> 00:07:15,696
... walked over to the bartender,
paid and left.

101
00:07:16,066 --> 00:07:17,943
The bartender lived?

102
00:07:22,146 --> 00:07:24,660
The bartender never gets killed.

103
00:07:26,146 --> 00:07:27,022
But...

104
00:07:28,826 --> 00:07:29,941
...as he neared the door....

105
00:07:36,866 --> 00:07:39,539
No, man, the bartender got it
worse than anybody.

106
00:07:44,466 --> 00:07:45,376
Here.

107
00:07:45,626 --> 00:07:46,854
It's on the house...

108
00:07:48,466 --> 00:07:50,024
...if you remember his face.

109
00:07:51,426 --> 00:07:53,462
Thanks, but no thanks.

110
00:07:54,226 --> 00:07:55,944
I'm clearing out of here.

111
00:07:56,186 --> 00:07:57,585
Because I think...

112
00:07:58,466 --> 00:07:59,819
...he's headed this way.

113
00:08:02,106 --> 00:08:03,016
Thank you, boys!

114
00:08:04,226 --> 00:08:05,625
Y'all take care!

115
00:09:42,386 --> 00:09:43,614
Get back.

116
00:09:46,026 --> 00:09:46,981
Stay back.

117
00:11:44,466 --> 00:11:45,694
Who is it?

118
00:11:46,146 --> 00:11:48,137
It's your only friend.

119
00:11:54,466 --> 00:11:57,458
Don't you think you're being
a little too cautious?

120
00:12:04,666 --> 00:12:07,897
One day you'll lay too hard on that
and blow your brains out.

121
00:12:11,146 --> 00:12:12,135
What do you want?

122
00:12:16,826 --> 00:12:17,781
He's there.

123
00:12:20,146 --> 00:12:22,614
I mentioned his name
and they freaked.

124
00:12:23,626 --> 00:12:24,695
Bucho's there?

125
00:12:25,266 --> 00:12:28,417
One second they weren't
listening to a word I said...

126
00:12:28,666 --> 00:12:30,418
...but when I mentioned him...

127
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:31,576
...they listened.

128
00:12:33,786 --> 00:12:36,858
And suddenly they got very interested
in who you were.

129
00:12:38,786 --> 00:12:41,254
So I laid the story down
nice and thick.

130
00:12:41,986 --> 00:12:43,101
How thick?

131
00:12:43,546 --> 00:12:44,581
Pretty thick.

132
00:12:44,786 --> 00:12:46,822
You were the biggest Mexican
I'd ever seen.

133
00:12:47,026 --> 00:12:47,981
Wonderful.

134
00:12:48,386 --> 00:12:50,342
I exaggerated, but they bought it.

135
00:12:50,586 --> 00:12:52,736
They're shitting bricks right now,
I promise.

136
00:12:52,986 --> 00:12:53,975
Where do I go?

137
00:12:57,786 --> 00:12:59,538
Tarasco Bar's a good start.

138
00:12:59,906 --> 00:13:02,659
Don't turn it into a bloodbath
like last time.

139
00:13:03,346 --> 00:13:04,665
That wasn't my fault.

140
00:13:04,906 --> 00:13:05,702
Of course not.

141
00:13:05,946 --> 00:13:06,901
They started it.

142
00:13:07,146 --> 00:13:08,977
Whatever. Just remember...

143
00:13:09,226 --> 00:13:12,377
...Bucho has plenty of thugs,
but without them, he's dead.

144
00:13:13,346 --> 00:13:14,301
Save your bullets.

145
00:13:14,786 --> 00:13:15,582
Suddenly...

146
00:13:16,906 --> 00:13:18,225
...you're my big brother.

147
00:13:19,186 --> 00:13:21,780
I do feel some responsibility for you.

148
00:13:24,146 --> 00:13:26,057
-Can I ask you something?
-What?

149
00:13:26,466 --> 00:13:28,058
What happens when he's dead?

150
00:13:30,906 --> 00:13:32,385
When Bucho's dead...

151
00:13:35,826 --> 00:13:37,100
...it's over.

152
00:13:39,346 --> 00:13:40,779
He's the last one.

153
00:13:42,026 --> 00:13:44,256
End of payback. Eye for an eye.

154
00:13:44,466 --> 00:13:46,661
You finally going to be satisfied?

155
00:13:47,746 --> 00:13:49,020
I think so.

156
00:13:49,826 --> 00:13:51,259
I hope so.

157
00:13:55,266 --> 00:13:57,860
I don't have the stomach
for this anymore.

158
00:13:59,266 --> 00:14:00,779
You never did.

159
00:14:02,466 --> 00:14:03,899
Neither did you.

160
00:15:39,186 --> 00:15:42,064
I just called the Oro Verde Bar in
Saragosa.

161
00:15:44,226 --> 00:15:46,023
There was no answer.

162
00:15:47,706 --> 00:15:49,776
Let me know if you hear anything.

163
00:15:54,906 --> 00:15:57,374
I want a close lookout
on all operations.

164
00:15:57,746 --> 00:16:01,216
That means double and triple checking,
even our regular customers.

165
00:16:01,466 --> 00:16:02,581
I'll handle it.

166
00:16:03,546 --> 00:16:06,424
Where's my car? ls it finished?
How long must I wait?

167
00:16:06,666 --> 00:16:07,940
I sent it back.

168
00:16:08,186 --> 00:16:11,064
Again? I could have built the thing
myself by now.

169
00:16:11,306 --> 00:16:13,297
-And what's this?
-It's my sister's nephew.

170
00:16:13,546 --> 00:16:16,822
He needs work, so he wanted to
show you his fighting abilities.

171
00:16:17,106 --> 00:16:20,576
You call this an audition,
fighting against Pipon?

172
00:16:21,066 --> 00:16:24,775
If he can't beat Cristos, I'm not
interested. Get in there.

173
00:16:25,826 --> 00:16:26,736
Get out!

174
00:16:44,986 --> 00:16:47,022
He doesn't look special so far.

175
00:16:48,946 --> 00:16:49,822
Kick his ass!

176
00:17:25,626 --> 00:17:27,264
That's more like it.

177
00:17:32,466 --> 00:17:33,865
He'll never dance again.

178
00:17:43,786 --> 00:17:46,425
-So much for Cristos.
-Told you.

179
00:17:46,666 --> 00:17:49,339
Listen. This is what I want you to do.

180
00:17:50,146 --> 00:17:53,138
Take extra men and place them
around the Tarasco and La Azteca.

181
00:17:53,386 --> 00:17:56,025
These Colombians wonder
if I can handle the extra volume.

182
00:17:56,266 --> 00:17:58,222
They're watching us enough as it is.

183
00:17:58,866 --> 00:17:59,935
-Hey.
-What?

184
00:18:00,186 --> 00:18:01,096
And him?

185
00:18:03,706 --> 00:18:07,176
Cast that leg up.
And welcome to the family.

186
00:19:29,706 --> 00:19:31,264
I have a house payment.

187
00:19:42,626 --> 00:19:43,581
Excuse me.

188
00:19:44,146 --> 00:19:45,101
But...

189
00:19:45,346 --> 00:19:46,938
...l used to work in a bar...

190
00:19:47,146 --> 00:19:49,706
...so I know what it's like
to wait on people.

191
00:19:49,946 --> 00:19:52,904
And I want to tell you
that the service here...

192
00:19:53,146 --> 00:19:55,580
...needs immediate improvement.

193
00:19:56,706 --> 00:19:58,139
What do you mean?

194
00:19:58,586 --> 00:19:59,814
What do I mean?

195
00:20:00,666 --> 00:20:01,860
Our waiter...

196
00:20:03,226 --> 00:20:04,181
...where is he?

197
00:20:06,546 --> 00:20:08,776
Don't tell me
he's still in the bathroom.

198
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:13,618
He never came back to see if we
wanted anything else.

199
00:20:13,986 --> 00:20:15,863
He never brought us our check.

200
00:20:16,186 --> 00:20:19,622
We wanted our check so we could
get the hell out of here.

201
00:20:22,226 --> 00:20:23,454
Here.

202
00:20:23,866 --> 00:20:25,424
This should be sufficient.

203
00:20:25,666 --> 00:20:27,896
And don't be expecting a tip.

204
00:20:29,586 --> 00:20:32,054
If you don't treat me good,
I won't ask you out.

205
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:35,176
And your beer tastes like piss.

206
00:20:35,426 --> 00:20:37,894
-We know!
-Because we piss in it!

207
00:20:38,346 --> 00:20:39,904
That's not all!

208
00:20:42,666 --> 00:20:43,815
Bad beer, bad service.

209
00:20:44,066 --> 00:20:45,465
Don't they know not to come in?

210
00:20:55,226 --> 00:20:56,136
2 cervezas.

211
00:20:57,786 --> 00:20:58,980
These are for you.

212
00:21:08,706 --> 00:21:09,821
Just a minute.

213
00:22:05,226 --> 00:22:06,864
I wanted to see the guitar.

214
00:22:10,786 --> 00:22:12,014
Do you play?

215
00:22:12,266 --> 00:22:14,143
Yes, do you?

216
00:22:14,586 --> 00:22:15,905
A little bit.

217
00:22:16,786 --> 00:22:18,185
Play something.

218
00:22:19,386 --> 00:22:20,819
Not right now.

219
00:22:21,226 --> 00:22:24,104
This is my father's,
but he doesn't play anymore.

220
00:22:24,506 --> 00:22:25,461
No?

221
00:22:25,986 --> 00:22:30,104
There's not much work for a mariachi.
Now he just watches TV.

222
00:22:31,986 --> 00:22:33,897
I'm sorry to hear that.

223
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:36,222
He was never that good anyway.

224
00:22:36,466 --> 00:22:38,821
Not as good as I'll be. Listen.

225
00:22:45,546 --> 00:22:47,138
Loosen your fingers a bit.

226
00:22:53,066 --> 00:22:54,260
Like this.

227
00:23:00,346 --> 00:23:01,745
You know what I mean?

228
00:23:02,986 --> 00:23:03,975
Loosen them up.

229
00:23:05,746 --> 00:23:07,065
How do you do that?

230
00:23:07,666 --> 00:23:08,815
All right.

231
00:23:10,346 --> 00:23:11,381
Give me this.

232
00:23:18,186 --> 00:23:20,984
Forget this hand, okay?
You want to get faster.

233
00:23:22,186 --> 00:23:23,221
Here's the secret.

234
00:23:28,346 --> 00:23:29,222
Got it?

235
00:23:29,466 --> 00:23:30,785
Good.

236
00:23:31,786 --> 00:23:33,378
Practice this...

237
00:23:35,266 --> 00:23:36,460
...every day.

238
00:23:39,466 --> 00:23:40,785
All day.

239
00:23:42,706 --> 00:23:43,616
Next time...

240
00:23:45,226 --> 00:23:47,137
...l'll show you how to play a tune...

241
00:23:47,386 --> 00:23:49,104
...using what you've learned.

242
00:23:52,826 --> 00:23:53,975
Practice.

243
00:24:18,866 --> 00:24:20,219
This reminds me of a joke.

244
00:24:22,306 --> 00:24:24,262
This guy comes into a bar...

245
00:24:24,586 --> 00:24:26,497
...walks to the bartender and says...

246
00:24:26,746 --> 00:24:29,055
..." Bartender, I got a bet for you.

247
00:24:29,506 --> 00:24:31,861
I'll bet you $300 that I can piss...

248
00:24:32,066 --> 00:24:33,977
...into that glass over there...

249
00:24:34,226 --> 00:24:35,579
...and not spill a drop."

250
00:24:36,986 --> 00:24:39,978
The bartender looks at the glass.
It's 1 0 feet away.

251
00:24:40,226 --> 00:24:41,215
He says...

252
00:24:41,466 --> 00:24:43,616
..."You're telling me
you'll bet me $300...

253
00:24:43,866 --> 00:24:45,697
...that you can piss,
standing here...

254
00:24:45,946 --> 00:24:48,938
...into that glass,
and not spill a single drop?"

255
00:24:50,066 --> 00:24:51,818
Customer looks up and says:

256
00:24:52,506 --> 00:24:53,734
"That's right."

257
00:24:54,146 --> 00:24:56,216
Bartender says, "You've got a bet."

258
00:24:56,466 --> 00:24:58,616
The guy goes, "Okay, here we go."

259
00:24:59,226 --> 00:25:00,898
Pulls out his thing.

260
00:25:01,146 --> 00:25:02,898
He's thinking about the glass.

261
00:25:03,146 --> 00:25:05,535
He's thinking about the glass.
Thinking about his dick.

262
00:25:05,866 --> 00:25:09,415
Dick, glass, dick, glass,
dick, glass, dick, glass.

263
00:25:09,666 --> 00:25:11,736
Then he lets it rip.

264
00:25:12,706 --> 00:25:15,015
He pisses all over the place.

265
00:25:15,266 --> 00:25:16,699
He pisses on the bar.

266
00:25:16,946 --> 00:25:20,018
He pisses on the stools,
on the floor, the phone.

267
00:25:20,706 --> 00:25:22,105
On the bartender!

268
00:25:22,626 --> 00:25:26,255
He's pissing everywhere
except the fucking glass!

269
00:25:29,106 --> 00:25:32,018
Bartender's laughing.
He's $300 richer. He's like....

270
00:25:32,946 --> 00:25:34,299
Piss dripping off his face.

271
00:25:34,626 --> 00:25:36,696
He says, "You fucking idiot, man!

272
00:25:36,946 --> 00:25:39,540
You got it in everything
except the glass!

273
00:25:40,226 --> 00:25:43,104
You owe me $300, puta."

274
00:25:44,386 --> 00:25:47,059
Guy goes, " Excuse me
just one little second."

275
00:25:47,306 --> 00:25:48,739
Goes in the back of the bar.

276
00:25:49,266 --> 00:25:51,541
There's a couple of guys
playing pool.

277
00:25:51,786 --> 00:25:53,014
He walks over to them.

278
00:25:53,906 --> 00:25:55,180
Comes back to the bar.

279
00:25:55,426 --> 00:25:57,781
Goes, " Here you go. $300."

280
00:25:58,706 --> 00:25:59,934
The bartender's like....

281
00:26:00,186 --> 00:26:03,144
"Why are you so happy?
You just lost $300, idiot!"

282
00:26:03,506 --> 00:26:05,861
The guy says,
"See those guys there?

283
00:26:07,226 --> 00:26:09,501
I just bet them $500 apiece...

284
00:26:10,706 --> 00:26:12,583
...that I could piss on your bar...

285
00:26:12,826 --> 00:26:15,898
...your floor, your phone,
and piss on you...

286
00:26:16,706 --> 00:26:20,016
...and not only would you not
be mad about it...

287
00:26:20,266 --> 00:26:21,858
...you'd be happy."

288
00:26:30,146 --> 00:26:31,545
That's funny shit, huh?

289
00:26:32,386 --> 00:26:34,741
"You'd be happy about it!"

290
00:26:39,866 --> 00:26:40,935
Guess what?

291
00:26:45,226 --> 00:26:46,420
He didn't check out.

292
00:26:47,666 --> 00:26:48,462
You...

293
00:26:50,226 --> 00:26:52,217
...you checked out just fine.

294
00:26:54,546 --> 00:26:57,060
Well, I knew I would because...

295
00:26:57,306 --> 00:26:58,534
...me and Bucco...

296
00:26:58,786 --> 00:26:59,980
-...we go way back.
-Bucho.

297
00:27:00,626 --> 00:27:01,615
Him too.

298
00:27:05,106 --> 00:27:06,221
And this guy....

299
00:27:06,466 --> 00:27:08,934
-I just met him today.
-Go on in.

300
00:27:09,186 --> 00:27:10,505
Good work, by the way.

301
00:27:10,746 --> 00:27:11,861
-Good work.
-Go in.

302
00:27:12,106 --> 00:27:14,620
It's nice to see you cross the I's
and dot the T's here.

303
00:27:14,866 --> 00:27:16,584
It's cool, ese, cool.

304
00:27:16,946 --> 00:27:17,981
Lead the way.

305
00:28:00,146 --> 00:28:01,499
In there?

306
00:28:03,226 --> 00:28:04,818
Fucking disgusting.

307
00:28:26,026 --> 00:28:27,254
What do you want?

308
00:28:29,346 --> 00:28:31,223
I'm just looking for work.

309
00:28:31,826 --> 00:28:33,179
There's no work here.

310
00:28:34,066 --> 00:28:35,385
I see.

311
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:43,058
Is there something to drink?

312
00:28:43,306 --> 00:28:44,978
Is there something in the case?

313
00:28:45,226 --> 00:28:46,454
Yeah.

314
00:28:46,706 --> 00:28:47,821
What?

315
00:28:48,306 --> 00:28:49,500
My guitar.

316
00:28:53,906 --> 00:28:57,103
Sure you don't want to hear me play
before you say there's no work?

317
00:28:57,786 --> 00:29:00,141
We just want to see
what's in the case.

318
00:29:00,626 --> 00:29:01,820
If it's like you say...

319
00:29:02,306 --> 00:29:03,580
...drink all you want.

320
00:29:07,266 --> 00:29:09,018
But I told you already.

321
00:29:09,426 --> 00:29:11,496
I'm a musician.
This is my guitar.

322
00:29:11,746 --> 00:29:12,701
Don't touch it!

323
00:29:13,226 --> 00:29:14,545
Get him away!

324
00:29:22,386 --> 00:29:23,341
Hurry.

325
00:29:24,626 --> 00:29:25,661
How you doing?

326
00:29:28,546 --> 00:29:29,422
What is it?

327
00:29:30,106 --> 00:29:31,175
It's a guitar.

328
00:29:35,426 --> 00:29:36,541
It's a guitar.

329
00:29:38,306 --> 00:29:40,456
We heard about a case full of guns.

330
00:29:40,706 --> 00:29:41,502
I know.

331
00:29:42,466 --> 00:29:44,024
Just had to make sure.

332
00:29:44,346 --> 00:29:45,142
I understand.

333
00:29:49,506 --> 00:29:50,700
It's him!

334
00:29:52,906 --> 00:29:53,975
Well, yes.

335
00:29:54,226 --> 00:29:55,136
It's me.

336
00:29:56,386 --> 00:29:58,695
I'm not against you, so keep it down.

337
00:29:58,946 --> 00:29:59,935
Keep it down.

338
00:30:01,066 --> 00:30:03,580
I'm just looking for a man who calls--

339
00:30:05,706 --> 00:30:07,105
Not yet.

340
00:30:35,866 --> 00:30:37,299
What the fuck's going on?!

341
00:30:40,146 --> 00:30:41,295
Is that going on now?

342
00:31:21,066 --> 00:31:22,181
Watch him!

343
00:31:22,506 --> 00:31:23,905
What the fuck's going on?

344
00:31:33,386 --> 00:31:34,455
Friends of yours?

345
00:31:35,706 --> 00:31:39,255
I swear I have no fucking idea
what the hell's going on!

346
00:31:52,386 --> 00:31:53,182
Shit!

347
00:32:37,506 --> 00:32:38,939
You missed me!

348
00:33:05,986 --> 00:33:07,260
Get up.

349
00:33:09,626 --> 00:33:10,775
Come here.

350
00:33:14,026 --> 00:33:17,814
I'm looking for a man who
calls himself " Bucho."

351
00:33:19,266 --> 00:33:20,255
That's all.

352
00:33:21,266 --> 00:33:23,826
But you had to do it the hard way.

353
00:33:29,986 --> 00:33:31,214
Listen to me.

354
00:33:32,266 --> 00:33:33,904
I don't want to kill you.

355
00:33:34,866 --> 00:33:37,824
I just want you to take me to him.
Understand?

356
00:33:48,426 --> 00:33:50,621
Tried to shoot me in the back, huh?!

357
00:33:59,066 --> 00:34:00,101
Fucker!

358
00:34:33,986 --> 00:34:35,385
If you want to go...

359
00:34:36,026 --> 00:34:36,822
...go.

360
00:34:38,826 --> 00:34:40,225
If you're going to stay...

361
00:34:41,786 --> 00:34:42,775
...relax.

362
00:34:59,826 --> 00:35:01,054
Fuck you!

363
00:38:13,786 --> 00:38:15,105
The money's still in back.

364
00:38:15,346 --> 00:38:16,665
So's the pickup.

365
00:38:16,866 --> 00:38:20,461
Pick-up Guy's lying on the floor
with 3 bullets in his head.

366
00:38:20,666 --> 00:38:23,134
-Tavo must have shot him.
-Where's Tavo?

367
00:38:23,746 --> 00:38:24,735
Tavo's outside.

368
00:38:25,826 --> 00:38:26,656
Where?

369
00:38:26,986 --> 00:38:27,975
2 blocks up.

370
00:38:28,186 --> 00:38:30,495
Tell him to get his ass over here!

371
00:38:30,706 --> 00:38:33,174
-I want to know what happened!
-He's dead.

372
00:39:06,506 --> 00:39:08,019
I'll tell you, boss...

373
00:39:08,986 --> 00:39:11,546
...whoever it was didn't
come for the money.

374
00:39:13,226 --> 00:39:14,739
They came for me.

375
00:39:17,026 --> 00:39:21,144
You've heard stories of the man
with a guitar case full of weapons.

376
00:39:22,186 --> 00:39:25,383
Those are stories.
That's all they are, stories.

377
00:39:25,586 --> 00:39:27,736
I cannot believe it.

378
00:39:33,266 --> 00:39:35,700
Can't you see we are fucking closed?!

379
00:39:38,626 --> 00:39:39,900
We need to find him.

380
00:39:40,106 --> 00:39:42,256
You said the Colombians are watching.

381
00:39:42,786 --> 00:39:43,980
So we move quickly.

382
00:39:44,226 --> 00:39:45,978
He's probably left town.

383
00:39:46,746 --> 00:39:48,259
He knows I'm here now.

384
00:39:48,506 --> 00:39:50,462
He's not going anywhere.

385
00:40:01,626 --> 00:40:02,900
Where am l?

386
00:40:03,546 --> 00:40:04,820
Bookstore.

387
00:40:05,546 --> 00:40:07,184
Bookstore-cafe.

388
00:40:12,786 --> 00:40:14,504
What the hell did you give me?

389
00:40:14,746 --> 00:40:16,099
Painkillers.

390
00:40:16,346 --> 00:40:17,415
I'm operating.

391
00:40:24,186 --> 00:40:25,585
Where is everybody?

392
00:40:26,106 --> 00:40:28,176
I closed early
so no one would come around.

393
00:40:28,426 --> 00:40:31,338
No one would come around anyway.

394
00:40:32,786 --> 00:40:33,696
Why?

395
00:40:34,146 --> 00:40:35,340
Nobody reads.

396
00:40:42,346 --> 00:40:44,382
Is it yours? All those...

397
00:40:44,626 --> 00:40:45,775
...books?

398
00:40:46,866 --> 00:40:48,015
It's mine.

399
00:40:48,266 --> 00:40:50,143
My parents passed away.

400
00:40:50,506 --> 00:40:52,940
They left me the building
and some money.

401
00:40:53,186 --> 00:40:54,619
I have an apartment upstairs.

402
00:40:58,186 --> 00:40:59,699
Why a bookstore?

403
00:40:59,946 --> 00:41:02,176
This town never had a bookstore.

404
00:41:03,306 --> 00:41:05,297
So I get this bright idea.

405
00:41:08,106 --> 00:41:10,540
Are you sure
you know what you're doing?

406
00:41:13,706 --> 00:41:15,059
Why a bookstore, huh?

407
00:41:15,866 --> 00:41:18,096
All right. Isn't there a hospital?

408
00:41:18,346 --> 00:41:21,463
Trust me. You don't want
to go to a hospital here.

409
00:41:24,586 --> 00:41:26,736
You'll never find work in this town.

410
00:41:27,746 --> 00:41:28,576
What?

411
00:41:29,186 --> 00:41:30,380
The guitar.

412
00:41:30,626 --> 00:41:32,423
Nobody hires musicians around here.

413
00:41:34,186 --> 00:41:35,301
I know.

414
00:41:37,746 --> 00:41:39,464
I use it to pick up girls.

415
00:41:45,546 --> 00:41:47,138
Oh, come on!

416
00:41:55,146 --> 00:41:56,625
-You see this?
-I see it.

417
00:41:57,826 --> 00:41:59,817
That one had your name on it.

418
00:42:02,786 --> 00:42:04,504
You don't even know my name.

419
00:42:04,866 --> 00:42:05,696
That's right.

420
00:42:06,426 --> 00:42:08,064
I don't know your name.

421
00:42:09,626 --> 00:42:10,820
You smoke?

422
00:42:13,306 --> 00:42:14,295
Nope.

423
00:42:21,866 --> 00:42:22,901
Thanks.

424
00:42:23,146 --> 00:42:25,979
It's the least I can do for you,
after saving my life.

425
00:42:27,146 --> 00:42:28,738
Have a couple more.

426
00:42:28,986 --> 00:42:30,897
-What is it?
-Painkillers.

427
00:42:34,386 --> 00:42:35,614
Hot water.

428
00:42:36,946 --> 00:42:37,856
Shit!

429
00:42:38,706 --> 00:42:39,582
What're you doing?!

430
00:42:39,826 --> 00:42:41,020
-Sorry.
-You're crazy.

431
00:42:41,266 --> 00:42:43,826
Relax. Here, this is the cold water.

432
00:42:49,946 --> 00:42:51,015
Better?

433
00:42:52,466 --> 00:42:53,615
Let's stitch you up.

434
00:43:20,866 --> 00:43:22,094
Get out of here!

435
00:44:35,786 --> 00:44:36,696
I know you.

436
00:44:37,866 --> 00:44:38,935
Really?

437
00:44:40,786 --> 00:44:43,539
You're that guy you always
hear stories about.

438
00:44:45,226 --> 00:44:46,625
You kill drug dealers.

439
00:44:46,866 --> 00:44:48,584
Do you know Bucho?

440
00:44:49,946 --> 00:44:52,938
I hope you don't think
you can take Bucho alone.

441
00:44:53,186 --> 00:44:54,016
You know him?

442
00:44:54,266 --> 00:44:55,255
Yeah.

443
00:44:56,786 --> 00:44:59,061
I have a few friends I can call.

444
00:44:59,306 --> 00:45:00,375
They owe me a favor.

445
00:45:02,186 --> 00:45:03,380
Don't complain.

446
00:45:03,706 --> 00:45:07,221
That would be straight if you hadn't
been moving so much.

447
00:45:07,946 --> 00:45:09,140
That one's worse.

448
00:45:09,386 --> 00:45:10,660
Who did that one?

449
00:45:11,026 --> 00:45:12,937
I did, a long time ago.

450
00:45:20,026 --> 00:45:22,256
I don't want to know what that is.

451
00:45:26,186 --> 00:45:29,223
Saved my life more than once.

452
00:45:30,866 --> 00:45:31,855
You can have it.

453
00:45:32,426 --> 00:45:33,859
No, thanks.

454
00:45:35,306 --> 00:45:36,898
No, I'm okay.

455
00:45:40,066 --> 00:45:41,294
Will you help me?

456
00:45:45,826 --> 00:45:47,782
I don't think I can help you.

457
00:45:49,626 --> 00:45:51,935
I must leave my things here
for a few minutes.

458
00:45:53,986 --> 00:45:54,782
Okay.

459
00:45:55,026 --> 00:45:56,345
I can trust you, right?

460
00:45:56,586 --> 00:45:57,416
Yeah.

461
00:45:57,666 --> 00:45:58,257
Really?

462
00:46:00,266 --> 00:46:01,301
All right.

463
00:46:02,026 --> 00:46:02,936
Where're you going?

464
00:46:03,186 --> 00:46:05,063
I have to go to church.

465
00:46:05,626 --> 00:46:06,661
What for?

466
00:46:06,906 --> 00:46:08,578
Confess my sins.

467
00:46:09,066 --> 00:46:10,260
I'm a sinner.

468
00:46:10,706 --> 00:46:11,616
I know.

469
00:46:17,946 --> 00:46:19,220
Did I thank you?

470
00:46:19,786 --> 00:46:21,219
No, you didn't.

471
00:46:24,106 --> 00:46:25,141
I will.

472
00:46:42,186 --> 00:46:43,539
What do you think?

473
00:46:45,866 --> 00:46:47,219
Bulletproof windows...

474
00:46:47,466 --> 00:46:48,740
...sidings...

475
00:46:48,986 --> 00:46:50,021
...the hood.

476
00:46:51,866 --> 00:46:53,185
Just what you asked for.

477
00:46:56,506 --> 00:46:57,461
Listen...

478
00:46:58,146 --> 00:47:01,422
...there are no more pickups today,
except one in Hidalgo.

479
00:47:01,666 --> 00:47:02,860
Stay away from there.

480
00:47:03,106 --> 00:47:06,735
The rest of the town is game.
Take this car and find him!

481
00:47:07,026 --> 00:47:07,936
I'll take my truck.

482
00:47:08,186 --> 00:47:10,063
Take the car. That's why I got it.

483
00:47:10,306 --> 00:47:11,944
If you see a stranger...

484
00:47:12,186 --> 00:47:14,984
...kill him. I can't take
any more chances.

485
00:47:19,906 --> 00:47:21,339
The sunroof's bulletproof.

486
00:47:21,586 --> 00:47:24,339
Works as a shield
when shooting out the top.

487
00:47:24,586 --> 00:47:25,939
Look at this guy.

488
00:47:31,626 --> 00:47:34,186
It works.
Now go and get him.

489
00:47:36,786 --> 00:47:40,620
I want you to take her.
You'll need all the help you can get.

490
00:47:54,866 --> 00:47:55,855
You too.

491
00:48:23,826 --> 00:48:26,977
Bless me, Father, for I have
just killed quite a few men.

492
00:48:27,226 --> 00:48:28,625
No shit.

493
00:48:29,466 --> 00:48:32,538
From what I hear, you cleaned out
the entire Tarasco Bar.

494
00:48:32,786 --> 00:48:36,142
Nice job. Every hit man
in Coahuila's looking for you.

495
00:48:36,386 --> 00:48:37,785
Things got out of hand.

496
00:48:38,346 --> 00:48:40,098
I said no more bloodbaths.

497
00:48:40,346 --> 00:48:43,179
I told you. Bucho's the last one.

498
00:48:44,346 --> 00:48:45,301
Then I'm finished.

499
00:48:45,546 --> 00:48:48,822
No, I'm finished.
They killed the woman you loved.

500
00:48:49,066 --> 00:48:50,784
Then they shot through your hand.

501
00:48:51,026 --> 00:48:52,937
Two points. Wake up!

502
00:48:53,186 --> 00:48:55,541
There is no payback for that.

503
00:48:56,946 --> 00:48:57,856
Walk away.

504
00:48:59,466 --> 00:49:00,216
Trust me...

505
00:49:00,466 --> 00:49:04,061
...this is one you won't
want to see through to the end.

506
00:49:05,826 --> 00:49:07,225
What do you mean?

507
00:49:07,946 --> 00:49:11,575
I've done some checking, and Bucho
is not someone to mess with.

508
00:49:11,826 --> 00:49:12,815
Trust me.

509
00:49:13,946 --> 00:49:15,504
I cannot leave without Bucho.

510
00:49:15,746 --> 00:49:18,544
You don't expect to live much longer?
Fine. I do.

511
00:49:18,786 --> 00:49:20,185
If you need any more help...

512
00:49:20,426 --> 00:49:21,495
...don't call me.

513
00:49:21,706 --> 00:49:24,095
Call Campa and Quino.
They're crazy.

514
00:49:24,346 --> 00:49:26,496
I should be able to count on you!

515
00:49:26,746 --> 00:49:28,338
Those days are gone.

516
00:49:28,786 --> 00:49:30,663
Just wait! Come on!

517
00:49:30,906 --> 00:49:33,022
Good luck. Don't get shot.

518
00:49:34,946 --> 00:49:36,504
Did you want confession?

519
00:49:39,986 --> 00:49:42,819
Maybe later, Father.
Because where I am going...

520
00:49:43,066 --> 00:49:45,102
...l'd just have to come right back.

521
00:50:11,066 --> 00:50:12,419
Look...

522
00:50:13,746 --> 00:50:16,499
...l didn't call about it before
because...

523
00:50:17,386 --> 00:50:18,535
...l could handle it.

524
00:50:20,786 --> 00:50:22,981
Yes, he's got no place to go.

525
00:50:23,746 --> 00:50:25,623
I got my men on him right now.

526
00:50:27,186 --> 00:50:28,904
You brought someone in?!

527
00:50:29,146 --> 00:50:30,943
How long has he been here?

528
00:50:31,466 --> 00:50:33,024
Who is he?

529
00:50:34,506 --> 00:50:37,339
What are you talking about?
We can handle it.

530
00:50:37,826 --> 00:50:40,294
Someone like that will
just tear the place up...

531
00:50:40,546 --> 00:50:42,423
...will make a lot of noise.

532
00:50:45,546 --> 00:50:47,298
What does your guy look like?

533
00:50:49,946 --> 00:50:53,177
I've got to know, or the wrong people
might get killed.

534
00:50:53,706 --> 00:50:57,619
Next time I'll call sooner,
but I knew I could handle this--

535
00:50:59,386 --> 00:51:00,421
Shit!

536
00:51:04,026 --> 00:51:06,460
What's the number
to the phone in my car?

537
00:51:08,346 --> 00:51:11,065
Fuckheads, what's the number
to my car phone?!

538
00:51:11,466 --> 00:51:12,501
Number!

539
00:51:15,626 --> 00:51:17,218
It's in your car, boss.

540
00:51:35,186 --> 00:51:38,861
What's the fucking number
to the phone in my car?

541
00:51:44,066 --> 00:51:44,976
Fuck.

542
00:51:47,986 --> 00:51:51,581
-What are you doing? Get away.
-You can't go away like this.

543
00:51:51,826 --> 00:51:52,576
I need you.

544
00:51:55,146 --> 00:51:56,704
I dreamt about her again.

545
00:51:56,946 --> 00:51:58,061
So what!

546
00:52:00,626 --> 00:52:01,581
Listen to me!

547
00:52:04,306 --> 00:52:05,421
You are right.

548
00:52:06,866 --> 00:52:07,855
You are right.

549
00:52:09,946 --> 00:52:11,140
Maybe I should quit.

550
00:52:11,546 --> 00:52:15,141
Now you're talking some sense,
because let me tell you...

551
00:52:15,386 --> 00:52:18,139
...you keep this up
and it'll be over real quick.

552
00:52:55,746 --> 00:52:56,656
Get in!

553
00:53:03,906 --> 00:53:04,577
Watch it!

554
00:53:13,946 --> 00:53:16,096
Where is he? We got to kill him.

555
00:54:05,466 --> 00:54:06,740
It's me again.

556
00:54:06,986 --> 00:54:09,898
The man you sent in--
What does he look like?

557
00:54:11,346 --> 00:54:14,418
Just so that I know.
So my people don't get confused.

558
00:54:15,506 --> 00:54:17,940
Dark hair, dark skin.
I figured that.

559
00:54:18,306 --> 00:54:20,024
Can I have a few more details?

560
00:54:20,826 --> 00:54:22,100
Tattoo on his chest.

561
00:54:23,866 --> 00:54:26,460
Tattoo of a woman on his chest.

562
00:54:26,666 --> 00:54:28,384
What else?

563
00:54:28,906 --> 00:54:29,975
Any weapons?

564
00:54:30,226 --> 00:54:31,784
Throwing knives.

565
00:54:33,586 --> 00:54:34,541
And...?

566
00:54:35,546 --> 00:54:39,539
And pay-phone money so he can
call you with progress reports.

567
00:54:40,986 --> 00:54:41,941
Yes, okay.

568
00:54:42,146 --> 00:54:43,864
That should do it, thanks.

569
00:54:46,106 --> 00:54:47,937
We'll stay out of his way.

570
00:54:48,506 --> 00:54:49,700
Yeah, thank you.

571
00:54:53,546 --> 00:54:54,535
Fuck!

572
00:54:54,786 --> 00:54:58,699
This is what I was talking about.
Our own people are watching us.

573
00:54:58,906 --> 00:55:01,374
He's been here since this morning,
checking on us.

574
00:55:02,506 --> 00:55:03,302
Bastards!

575
00:55:03,986 --> 00:55:05,135
Go find him!

576
00:55:05,346 --> 00:55:06,222
Go and find who?

577
00:55:06,626 --> 00:55:07,741
There's no one else!

578
00:55:07,946 --> 00:55:11,859
He is claimed as a Colombian.
They won't admit they're after you.

579
00:55:12,386 --> 00:55:16,299
There's someone else out there.
And I want to find him now!

580
00:55:16,546 --> 00:55:17,774
Who else is there?

581
00:55:18,106 --> 00:55:19,380
The guitar player?

582
00:55:19,626 --> 00:55:20,979
The guy is a myth.

583
00:55:21,346 --> 00:55:24,179
-A myth.
-You are not a believer.

584
00:55:24,466 --> 00:55:26,422
That will be your downfall.

585
00:55:26,666 --> 00:55:29,385
I'm going with you.
I can't leave this up to you.

586
00:55:30,746 --> 00:55:32,896
Now my ass is on the line.

587
00:55:49,506 --> 00:55:50,302
Manito!

588
00:55:50,826 --> 00:55:52,544
Why aren't you practicing?

589
00:55:52,986 --> 00:55:55,625
I told you, man.
Every day, all day.

590
00:55:56,466 --> 00:55:58,024
I can't play this guitar.

591
00:55:59,666 --> 00:56:00,701
Come on.

592
00:56:00,946 --> 00:56:02,140
Where are you going?

593
00:56:02,466 --> 00:56:04,263
I'm going to get my guitar.

594
00:56:04,826 --> 00:56:05,941
I'll wait here.

595
00:56:06,146 --> 00:56:07,784
It's right over there.

596
00:56:08,746 --> 00:56:09,940
What's over there?

597
00:56:10,146 --> 00:56:13,138
My guitar. I want to show you
I've been practicing.

598
00:56:22,746 --> 00:56:23,940
Stupid kid.

599
00:56:51,426 --> 00:56:54,179
Stay there.
No one else is supposed to be here.

600
00:56:59,546 --> 00:57:01,138
See? Here it comes.

601
00:57:17,066 --> 00:57:19,341
See? Now this one I can play.

602
00:57:29,386 --> 00:57:30,819
Don't even think about it.

603
00:57:32,506 --> 00:57:33,621
Give me the guitar.

604
00:57:34,666 --> 00:57:35,576
The guitar!

605
00:57:38,906 --> 00:57:39,656
Go away.

606
00:57:47,786 --> 00:57:48,901
Shit.

607
00:57:58,946 --> 00:58:00,777
This your father's guitar?

608
00:58:02,786 --> 00:58:04,617
Is this why he doesn't work now?

609
00:58:04,826 --> 00:58:06,737
They switch guitars every few days.

610
00:58:06,946 --> 00:58:08,174
What do you get?

611
00:58:08,386 --> 00:58:11,776
My father doesn't have to work.
He watches TV.

612
00:58:11,986 --> 00:58:13,385
He says they hide it all over.

613
00:58:13,586 --> 00:58:16,259
Ladies with baby carriages,
the church...

614
00:58:16,506 --> 00:58:18,497
...bookstores. Ask Carolina.

615
00:58:18,706 --> 00:58:19,502
She'll tell you.

616
00:58:19,706 --> 00:58:20,900
She does the same thing.

617
00:58:38,026 --> 00:58:39,425
What? Jesus.

618
00:58:39,666 --> 00:58:41,463
-What did you tell him?!
-Who?

619
00:58:41,706 --> 00:58:44,379
-You work for him, right?
-I work for nobody.

620
00:58:44,626 --> 00:58:46,378
I want to know what you said!

621
00:58:46,626 --> 00:58:47,979
-Nothing.
-Nothing?!

622
00:58:48,226 --> 00:58:49,978
What are you talking about?!

623
00:58:50,226 --> 00:58:51,136
You said I was at church!

624
00:58:51,346 --> 00:58:54,144
-I haven't said anything to anybody!
-Look at me now!

625
00:58:54,386 --> 00:58:55,660
You're protecting him!

626
00:58:55,866 --> 00:58:56,855
-I'm not!
-You are!

627
00:58:57,106 --> 00:58:59,904
If I was, I would've
told him you were here!

628
00:59:00,186 --> 00:59:00,936
You don't want him dead!

629
00:59:01,146 --> 00:59:04,695
I want no one dead!
Killing him is not the answer.

630
00:59:04,946 --> 00:59:05,742
See?!

631
00:59:05,986 --> 00:59:07,021
You know what I see?

632
00:59:07,266 --> 00:59:09,382
I see you are no better than he is.

633
00:59:11,146 --> 00:59:12,625
The same shit!

634
00:59:19,346 --> 00:59:20,574
Anybody can be bought.

635
00:59:20,826 --> 00:59:22,145
Not anybody.

636
00:59:22,386 --> 00:59:23,614
You're so good, huh?

637
00:59:23,866 --> 00:59:26,061
You see this bookstore? It's mine.

638
00:59:26,266 --> 00:59:28,541
Somebody comes
and drops something off.

639
00:59:28,786 --> 00:59:30,538
-A couple of days later...
-How much?

640
00:59:30,746 --> 00:59:32,304
...somebody else comes to
pick it up.

641
00:59:32,506 --> 00:59:33,461
I rent space!

642
00:59:33,666 --> 00:59:35,384
-That's all I do.
-How much?!

643
00:59:35,586 --> 00:59:36,496
The back room.

644
00:59:36,706 --> 00:59:38,458
How much does he pay you?

645
00:59:42,626 --> 00:59:43,979
$50,000 a year.

646
00:59:44,186 --> 00:59:46,177
$50,000.

647
00:59:49,066 --> 00:59:49,942
Cash.

648
00:59:59,386 --> 01:00:02,344
Look at you. You're a mess again.
Come here.

649
01:00:11,826 --> 01:00:12,861
On the counter.

650
01:00:18,706 --> 01:00:21,266
I didn't open this place
just to see it fail.

651
01:00:21,466 --> 01:00:24,105
It wasn't making any money.
I would've had to close.

652
01:00:24,306 --> 01:00:27,821
One day, Bucho walks in
with a suitcase full of money...

653
01:00:28,066 --> 01:00:30,455
...and says to me,
" Carolina, take this...

654
01:00:30,666 --> 01:00:32,338
...and go about your business...

655
01:00:32,626 --> 01:00:35,459
...and I will give you $50,000 a year."

656
01:00:39,626 --> 01:00:41,856
They've done it with
a lot of people here.

657
01:00:42,066 --> 01:00:44,341
They use our business as fronts.

658
01:00:44,946 --> 01:00:47,858
I used some of the money
to keep this place open.

659
01:00:48,106 --> 01:00:50,256
And I stashed the rest, thinking...

660
01:00:50,626 --> 01:00:51,945
...if some day...

661
01:00:52,186 --> 01:00:54,541
...things got really bad here...

662
01:00:54,786 --> 01:00:56,742
...l'd have the money to leave.

663
01:00:57,546 --> 01:00:59,025
But I can't leave.

664
01:00:59,946 --> 01:01:02,506
Because once you're in,
you can't get out.

665
01:01:02,786 --> 01:01:05,300
The closest thing I had to a brother...

666
01:01:05,786 --> 01:01:07,378
...was just killed.

667
01:01:08,386 --> 01:01:10,820
I cannot stop what it is I have to do.

668
01:01:11,586 --> 01:01:12,735
I cannot.

669
01:01:15,026 --> 01:01:15,742
Damn it!

670
01:01:24,866 --> 01:01:26,424
Do you need some help?

671
01:01:26,666 --> 01:01:28,861
No. I was trying to move my...

672
01:01:29,426 --> 01:01:30,859
...my cash register.

673
01:01:31,746 --> 01:01:33,338
I needed a new one anyway.

674
01:01:42,466 --> 01:01:43,819
So...

675
01:01:44,506 --> 01:01:45,825
...what brings you here?

676
01:01:46,346 --> 01:01:48,780
I don't come around much anymore,
do l?

677
01:01:50,786 --> 01:01:51,980
No.

678
01:01:53,506 --> 01:01:54,734
How've you been?

679
01:01:55,106 --> 01:01:56,380
Been okay.

680
01:01:56,786 --> 01:01:57,901
Business?

681
01:01:58,146 --> 01:01:59,738
Business is good.

682
01:02:01,666 --> 01:02:03,384
About as good as it can be.

683
01:02:05,026 --> 01:02:06,425
I told you...

684
01:02:06,666 --> 01:02:07,416
...bookstores....

685
01:02:09,626 --> 01:02:11,025
Not in this town.

686
01:02:11,946 --> 01:02:13,174
And you?

687
01:02:17,626 --> 01:02:21,380
I'm looking for someone
that's threatening our business.

688
01:02:21,586 --> 01:02:23,861
You may have heard
about the bar today.

689
01:02:24,066 --> 01:02:26,534
Oh, yeah. There was a shooting.

690
01:02:26,866 --> 01:02:29,858
Have you seen anyone around
that may look--

691
01:02:30,106 --> 01:02:30,777
Suspicious?

692
01:02:37,306 --> 01:02:38,421
No.

693
01:02:41,786 --> 01:02:42,980
Fuck.

694
01:02:43,226 --> 01:02:46,855
The guy I'm looking for
is obviously dangerous...

695
01:02:49,306 --> 01:02:51,900
...so I'm not asking you
to confront him...

696
01:02:52,986 --> 01:02:53,975
...but...

697
01:02:54,186 --> 01:02:55,062
...if you see him...

698
01:02:57,466 --> 01:02:58,945
...will you call me?

699
01:02:59,986 --> 01:03:01,021
Sure.

700
01:03:04,586 --> 01:03:05,496
I mean...

701
01:03:14,066 --> 01:03:16,626
...we can't have any more shootings.

702
01:03:25,986 --> 01:03:27,578
But I haven't seen him.

703
01:03:34,066 --> 01:03:35,340
You...

704
01:03:35,586 --> 01:03:37,065
...wouldn't lie to me...

705
01:03:37,306 --> 01:03:38,341
...would you?

706
01:03:44,866 --> 01:03:45,776
No.

707
01:03:50,466 --> 01:03:52,263
That's some mess you've got.

708
01:03:52,946 --> 01:03:53,822
Yeah.

709
01:03:58,346 --> 01:03:59,574
I better clean it up.

710
01:04:01,506 --> 01:04:03,542
Thank you for the coffee.
Call me.

711
01:04:03,826 --> 01:04:05,100
Yes...

712
01:04:06,146 --> 01:04:07,738
...if I see him...

713
01:04:08,506 --> 01:04:10,224
...l'll be sure to call you.

714
01:04:13,426 --> 01:04:14,779
Call me.

715
01:04:20,586 --> 01:04:21,735
Was that him?

716
01:04:21,946 --> 01:04:25,143
You're not doing anything to him here
or we'll both be killed.

717
01:04:25,386 --> 01:04:27,422
And I don't want to die over this.

718
01:04:28,946 --> 01:04:30,698
Stay away from the window.

719
01:05:23,306 --> 01:05:25,103
This one's not so bad.

720
01:05:29,386 --> 01:05:31,661
Actually, it's almost straight.

721
01:05:34,026 --> 01:05:35,664
Why didn't you tell him...

722
01:05:35,906 --> 01:05:37,305
...l was here?

723
01:05:39,626 --> 01:05:40,775
I don't know.

724
01:05:42,786 --> 01:05:45,380
I know you think
he's a terrible person.

725
01:05:47,026 --> 01:05:48,505
Honey, he is.

726
01:05:50,586 --> 01:05:51,735
He is.

727
01:05:53,026 --> 01:05:54,618
Not really.

728
01:05:55,226 --> 01:05:56,864
He's got a good side to him.

729
01:05:57,066 --> 01:05:59,660
And that's the only thing
that can save him.

730
01:06:05,306 --> 01:06:06,500
What is this?

731
01:06:07,266 --> 01:06:08,858
That was for you.

732
01:06:09,186 --> 01:06:10,824
It was for me?

733
01:06:11,066 --> 01:06:12,784
It's not for me anymore?

734
01:06:13,906 --> 01:06:15,578
Okay, you can have it.

735
01:06:19,506 --> 01:06:22,623
I didn't get you a case,
since you already have one.

736
01:06:22,866 --> 01:06:24,743
It's beautiful. Thank you.

737
01:06:24,986 --> 01:06:26,419
And I was thinking maybe...

738
01:06:26,666 --> 01:06:30,454
...you can clear out the guns
and put this in instead.

739
01:06:31,906 --> 01:06:32,941
Maybe.

740
01:06:33,986 --> 01:06:35,214
Play something.

741
01:06:35,466 --> 01:06:36,296
No.

742
01:06:36,546 --> 01:06:38,343
Come on, let me help you.

743
01:06:41,706 --> 01:06:43,105
-I'm sorry.
-Be careful.

744
01:06:43,626 --> 01:06:44,695
It's okay.

745
01:06:45,386 --> 01:06:47,456
No, I can't play anymore.

746
01:06:47,986 --> 01:06:48,736
Why?

747
01:06:48,986 --> 01:06:50,942
Well, look at my hand. It's....

748
01:06:52,426 --> 01:06:53,302
I can't.

749
01:06:53,546 --> 01:06:55,218
We can improvise.

750
01:06:55,466 --> 01:06:56,865
Improvise?

751
01:06:59,706 --> 01:07:00,775
Do you play?

752
01:07:02,866 --> 01:07:04,060
A little.

753
01:07:05,746 --> 01:07:06,781
All right.

754
01:07:11,506 --> 01:07:13,303
That's not even a note.

755
01:07:14,146 --> 01:07:15,818
Let me show you.

756
01:07:16,066 --> 01:07:18,057
Put these fingers over here.

757
01:07:18,386 --> 01:07:19,535
Like this?

758
01:07:20,266 --> 01:07:22,018
Good. That's nice.

759
01:07:22,266 --> 01:07:23,381
Let me see.

760
01:07:38,266 --> 01:07:39,176
All right.

761
01:09:36,786 --> 01:09:37,775
Memo...

762
01:09:38,266 --> 01:09:39,699
...he's in the bookstore.

763
01:09:40,266 --> 01:09:41,665
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

764
01:09:43,386 --> 01:09:47,379
Check it out anyway. If he's in there,
and she's hiding him...

765
01:09:47,626 --> 01:09:48,854
...kill them both.

766
01:09:49,186 --> 01:09:51,017
Make it look like an accident.

767
01:09:52,266 --> 01:09:53,938
It's a bookstore.

768
01:09:54,186 --> 01:09:55,619
Burn it down.

769
01:12:04,666 --> 01:12:05,815
Move!

770
01:12:08,266 --> 01:12:08,937
Come on!

771
01:12:09,586 --> 01:12:10,416
Hurry!

772
01:12:10,946 --> 01:12:11,696
Take this!

773
01:12:12,026 --> 01:12:13,095
Do what?

774
01:12:16,866 --> 01:12:17,855
Come on!

775
01:12:18,066 --> 01:12:18,816
What!

776
01:12:19,026 --> 01:12:20,175
I must get my purse!

777
01:12:20,426 --> 01:12:21,381
Fuck it!

778
01:12:23,906 --> 01:12:24,577
Wait!

779
01:12:25,346 --> 01:12:26,062
Wait!

780
01:12:26,546 --> 01:12:27,342
Here.

781
01:12:30,946 --> 01:12:32,425
You look great.

782
01:12:33,666 --> 01:12:34,735
Thank you.

783
01:12:36,466 --> 01:12:37,455
Where're we going?

784
01:12:37,706 --> 01:12:39,105
Downstairs, out the front.

785
01:12:39,306 --> 01:12:40,261
Take this.

786
01:12:47,346 --> 01:12:48,779
Jesus Christ!

787
01:12:51,666 --> 01:12:52,894
What are you doing?!

788
01:12:55,346 --> 01:12:56,779
Get out of here!

789
01:13:06,786 --> 01:13:07,821
Let's go!

790
01:13:39,546 --> 01:13:41,298
Go! Go! Go!

791
01:14:03,906 --> 01:14:04,941
You okay?

792
01:14:35,586 --> 01:14:37,417
I'm sorry, Carolina.

793
01:14:39,146 --> 01:14:40,374
I'm sorry.

794
01:14:49,266 --> 01:14:50,381
That's him.

795
01:14:50,666 --> 01:14:51,462
What?

796
01:14:53,786 --> 01:14:54,980
That's Bucho?

797
01:15:07,426 --> 01:15:09,576
I can shoot him from here.

798
01:15:12,626 --> 01:15:13,661
Motherfucker.

799
01:15:36,946 --> 01:15:37,935
What?

800
01:15:43,986 --> 01:15:45,658
What are you doing?

801
01:15:45,866 --> 01:15:46,742
Shoot him.

802
01:15:46,986 --> 01:15:47,657
Shoot him!

803
01:15:49,746 --> 01:15:51,782
My whole life was in there.

804
01:15:56,226 --> 01:15:57,625
Can't you see?

805
01:15:57,866 --> 01:16:00,221
Can't you see?
He's going to kill me.

806
01:16:00,426 --> 01:16:01,495
Come on!

807
01:16:02,986 --> 01:16:03,657
Damn!

808
01:16:09,946 --> 01:16:12,619
What's wrong?
You had the perfect chance!

809
01:16:13,426 --> 01:16:16,145
What's the matter?
Why didn't you shoot him?

810
01:16:23,506 --> 01:16:24,461
Come on.

811
01:16:24,946 --> 01:16:25,935
Come on.

812
01:16:27,466 --> 01:16:28,455
Come on!

813
01:16:39,266 --> 01:16:40,699
Wait a minute!

814
01:16:50,706 --> 01:16:51,980
It's one thing...

815
01:16:52,186 --> 01:16:55,337
...if you can't find someone
running around the city...

816
01:16:55,946 --> 01:16:57,937
...hiding anyplace he chooses.

817
01:16:58,546 --> 01:17:00,218
I can understand that.

818
01:17:00,466 --> 01:17:02,900
Now what I can't understand is...

819
01:17:03,226 --> 01:17:06,741
...how can you let him get away
when you knew where he was?

820
01:17:07,586 --> 01:17:09,178
You drive around town...

821
01:17:09,386 --> 01:17:11,342
...you see someone you don't know,
shoot them.

822
01:17:11,546 --> 01:17:13,025
How hard is that?

823
01:17:24,266 --> 01:17:25,494
Look over there.

824
01:17:28,386 --> 01:17:29,341
I don't know him.

825
01:17:30,546 --> 01:17:32,138
Never seen him before.

826
01:17:32,946 --> 01:17:33,696
A gun!

827
01:17:34,906 --> 01:17:36,464
It must be him.

828
01:17:39,666 --> 01:17:41,497
Now, how hard is that?

829
01:17:44,306 --> 01:17:45,978
It's that easy.

830
01:17:53,146 --> 01:17:53,942
Look!

831
01:17:54,146 --> 01:17:55,579
Who are those guys?

832
01:17:55,826 --> 01:17:57,418
I've never seen them.

833
01:18:04,226 --> 01:18:05,739
Now, how hard is that?

834
01:18:09,306 --> 01:18:10,136
Bang!

835
01:18:10,666 --> 01:18:13,499
Can you handle that?
Or I got to do everything myself?

836
01:18:13,706 --> 01:18:14,821
I'll handle it.

837
01:18:16,386 --> 01:18:18,024
Bet your ass you will.

838
01:18:18,386 --> 01:18:21,139
Take my car!
That's what I bought it for!

839
01:18:22,906 --> 01:18:24,055
Stay here.

840
01:18:24,266 --> 01:18:26,700
I need someone competent
guarding this place!

841
01:18:29,186 --> 01:18:30,255
Hurry up!

842
01:18:59,506 --> 01:19:01,736
I wasn't always like this.

843
01:19:02,826 --> 01:19:04,384
I can see that.

844
01:19:13,746 --> 01:19:14,735
I was a musician.

845
01:19:15,906 --> 01:19:17,180
Were you any good?

846
01:19:17,746 --> 01:19:19,099
I was okay.

847
01:19:22,946 --> 01:19:24,618
They shot my hand.

848
01:19:26,626 --> 01:19:27,661
You know...

849
01:19:28,906 --> 01:19:32,057
...it's easier to pull the trigger
than play guitar.

850
01:19:34,186 --> 01:19:36,746
Easier to destroy than to create.

851
01:19:41,386 --> 01:19:43,342
They killed the woman I loved.

852
01:19:47,186 --> 01:19:48,824
They ruined my life.

853
01:19:52,826 --> 01:19:55,260
Bucho's men were responsible for it.

854
01:20:04,306 --> 01:20:06,866
Why didn't you kill Bucho?

855
01:20:07,506 --> 01:20:08,541
All right...

856
01:20:10,546 --> 01:20:11,945
...here's the plan:

857
01:20:14,306 --> 01:20:17,457
You can still get away
without me having to kill him.

858
01:20:18,906 --> 01:20:19,975
You have money.

859
01:20:20,226 --> 01:20:21,579
There is no money.

860
01:20:22,626 --> 01:20:23,536
What?

861
01:20:23,786 --> 01:20:24,855
It's gone.

862
01:20:25,066 --> 01:20:27,341
I had it hidden in the books.

863
01:20:27,786 --> 01:20:28,855
It burned.

864
01:20:29,226 --> 01:20:30,625
Oh, shit.

865
01:20:31,826 --> 01:20:34,260
I have nothing. Nothing.

866
01:20:34,506 --> 01:20:35,621
Oh, great.

867
01:20:36,026 --> 01:20:37,175
Shit!

868
01:20:43,346 --> 01:20:45,382
What about calling your friends?

869
01:20:47,226 --> 01:20:48,375
Campa.

870
01:20:49,906 --> 01:20:50,975
Quino.

871
01:20:52,626 --> 01:20:54,105
They'd destroy the city.

872
01:20:54,306 --> 01:20:56,900
Bucho would still get away.
Forget it.

873
01:21:09,386 --> 01:21:11,536
It may not matter to you...

874
01:21:13,226 --> 01:21:16,423
...but he'll follow me everywhere I go
until I'm dead.

875
01:21:17,266 --> 01:21:18,665
It does matter to me.

876
01:21:41,786 --> 01:21:42,855
Campa?

877
01:21:44,306 --> 01:21:45,705
Is Quino there?

878
01:21:48,426 --> 01:21:51,384
How fast can the two of you
get to Santa Cecilia?

879
01:21:51,626 --> 01:21:52,979
I'll be looking for you.

880
01:21:53,706 --> 01:21:54,661
Thanks.

881
01:21:56,746 --> 01:21:57,701
Campa...

882
01:21:59,066 --> 01:22:00,499
...bring your guitars.

883
01:22:32,746 --> 01:22:34,338
Give me the strength...

884
01:22:34,746 --> 01:22:36,338
...to be what I was.

885
01:22:38,346 --> 01:22:40,416
And forgive me for what I am.

886
01:24:02,666 --> 01:24:04,338
Back together again, eh?

887
01:24:08,506 --> 01:24:09,621
Let's play.

888
01:27:01,266 --> 01:27:02,255
Cover yourself!

889
01:27:06,786 --> 01:27:07,457
Fuck!

890
01:28:56,426 --> 01:28:58,735
I'm not sure this is the place.

891
01:28:59,266 --> 01:29:00,938
This is the place.

892
01:29:09,226 --> 01:29:10,739
I'm going with you.

893
01:29:40,986 --> 01:29:41,941
Manito.

894
01:29:44,426 --> 01:29:46,337
What are you doing here?

895
01:29:48,026 --> 01:29:50,984
I thought I was looking for
the devil himself.

896
01:29:53,146 --> 01:29:56,536
And all this time
it was my own brother.

897
01:30:00,426 --> 01:30:02,576
I didn't know it was you.

898
01:30:03,066 --> 01:30:05,182
I only found out this morning.

899
01:30:14,026 --> 01:30:16,381
I ought to kill you right now.

900
01:30:16,986 --> 01:30:18,499
You disgraced me.

901
01:30:18,746 --> 01:30:21,055
We always knew you were up to no good.

902
01:30:21,346 --> 01:30:22,699
Never thought you'd go this far.

903
01:30:22,946 --> 01:30:25,141
So my little brother comes here...

904
01:30:25,346 --> 01:30:26,540
...to teach me a lesson.

905
01:30:26,786 --> 01:30:28,902
Show me what's right from wrong.

906
01:30:29,866 --> 01:30:31,584
You are a guitar player.

907
01:30:31,866 --> 01:30:35,302
What are you doing killing my men,
ruining my business?!

908
01:30:35,546 --> 01:30:37,298
They killed the woman I loved.

909
01:30:37,546 --> 01:30:39,776
You killed them!
What do you want?

910
01:30:40,226 --> 01:30:42,262
I don't set out to kill innocent people.

911
01:30:42,506 --> 01:30:44,224
You just buy innocent people.

912
01:30:44,746 --> 01:30:46,020
You don't kill them...

913
01:30:46,226 --> 01:30:48,023
...until you have no use for them.

914
01:30:50,066 --> 01:30:51,943
Isn't she the woman you love now?

915
01:30:52,146 --> 01:30:53,977
When we take away something...

916
01:30:54,226 --> 01:30:55,784
...we replace it.

917
01:30:56,226 --> 01:30:58,262
She's a real piece of work.

918
01:30:58,506 --> 01:31:00,178
Trust me. I know.

919
01:31:00,386 --> 01:31:01,580
Sorry about the bookstore.

920
01:31:01,786 --> 01:31:03,777
I always said
it would go up in smoke.

921
01:31:04,426 --> 01:31:08,385
Had I known it was my brother you were
fucking, I'd have acted differently.

922
01:31:08,586 --> 01:31:09,496
Cesar...

923
01:31:10,786 --> 01:31:13,095
...l've learned to read the eyes of men.

924
01:31:13,306 --> 01:31:15,024
What do you read in mine?

925
01:31:15,746 --> 01:31:17,498
Defeat, brother.

926
01:31:18,306 --> 01:31:19,216
Defeat?

927
01:31:19,626 --> 01:31:20,945
Look at you.

928
01:31:21,626 --> 01:31:23,537
You came here to kill me.

929
01:31:23,906 --> 01:31:25,976
Papa wouldn't be proud of you anymore.

930
01:31:26,266 --> 01:31:28,382
You were his little guitarrista.

931
01:31:28,626 --> 01:31:29,979
His little mariachi.

932
01:31:30,786 --> 01:31:31,901
And now...

933
01:31:32,146 --> 01:31:34,341
...just a piece of shit like me!

934
01:31:35,986 --> 01:31:37,419
You want to kill me?

935
01:31:37,666 --> 01:31:38,985
Let me tell you something.

936
01:31:39,226 --> 01:31:40,944
You have already killed me!

937
01:31:41,986 --> 01:31:43,817
Put your hands up, manito.

938
01:31:46,266 --> 01:31:47,176
Let's go.

939
01:31:47,386 --> 01:31:48,421
Put them up!

940
01:31:51,386 --> 01:31:52,262
I'm sorry.

941
01:31:52,866 --> 01:31:56,176
But I can't have you acting heroic
when I punish Carolina...

942
01:31:56,426 --> 01:31:57,575
...for betraying me.

943
01:31:57,786 --> 01:31:59,902
But let me do this
and we'll be even.

944
01:32:00,346 --> 01:32:02,064
Clean slate.

945
01:32:02,506 --> 01:32:04,462
You killed my men. Okay.

946
01:32:04,666 --> 01:32:05,781
What's done is done.

947
01:32:06,266 --> 01:32:07,858
I'm finished anyway.

948
01:32:08,106 --> 01:32:09,300
But now...

949
01:32:10,266 --> 01:32:11,585
...l kill Carolina.

950
01:32:13,466 --> 01:32:15,422
And you get to watch.

951
01:32:24,786 --> 01:32:25,980
Goodbye, Carolina.

952
01:32:34,786 --> 01:32:36,538
Everyone I've killed...

953
01:32:38,146 --> 01:32:39,943
...was someone's father...

954
01:32:41,186 --> 01:32:42,858
...someone's son...

955
01:32:45,586 --> 01:32:47,258
...someone's brother.

956
01:32:59,946 --> 01:33:00,935
Practice.

957
01:33:17,586 --> 01:33:18,860
Where are you going?

958
01:33:22,066 --> 01:33:23,340
I don't know.

959
01:33:40,426 --> 01:33:41,575
Carolina?

960
01:33:43,546 --> 01:33:44,774
Did I thank you?

961
01:33:46,786 --> 01:33:47,741
No.

962
01:33:50,826 --> 01:33:51,895
I will.

963
01:34:32,346 --> 01:34:33,540
So....

964
01:34:33,986 --> 01:34:36,261
I want you to thank me right now.

965
01:34:56,506 --> 01:34:57,655
Thank you.

966
01:35:23,906 --> 01:35:25,544
Just in case.

967
01:35:27,106 --> 01:35:29,381
It's a long ride to the next town.
